  "content": {
    "id": "p10-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Recall that the range of $f(x)=\\sqrt{x}$ is $y\\ge 0$ because $\\sqrt{x}$ cannot be negative. Use this fact to determine the range of the following.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p10-q13-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=2\\sqrt{x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y\\ge 0$",
          "worked": "Since $\\sqrt{x}\\ge 0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}2\\sqrt{x}&\\ge 0\\\\y&\\ge 0.\\end{align*}$$\nThe minimum is attained at $x=0$, and there is no upper bound.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q13-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\sqrt{x}+3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y\\ge 3$",
          "worked": "Since $\\sqrt{x}\\ge 0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sqrt{x}+3&\\ge 3\\\\y&\\ge 3.\\end{align*}$$\nThe minimum is attained at $x=0$, and there is no upper bound.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q13-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\sqrt{x}-5$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y\\ge -5$",
          "worked": "Since $\\sqrt{x}\\ge 0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sqrt{x}-5&\\ge -5\\\\y&\\ge -5.\\end{align*}$$\nThe minimum is attained at $x=0$, and there is no upper bound.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q13-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=-\\sqrt{x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y\\le 0$",
          "worked": "Since $\\sqrt{x}\\ge 0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}-\\sqrt{x}&\\le 0\\\\y&\\le 0.\\end{align*}$$\nThe maximum is attained at $x=0$, and there is no lower bound.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q13-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=-\\sqrt{x}+4$",
